# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<script setup>
import * as vue from "vue";
import { set as s, del as d } from "vue";

s(obj, key, value);
d(obj, key);
vue.set(obj, key, value);
vue.del(obj, key);
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-script-setup.vue:6:1 lint/nursery/noVueDeprecatedDeleteSet ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This calls the Vue set function, which Vue 3 removed.
  
    4 │ import { set as s, del as d } from "vue";
    5 │ 
  > 6 │ s(obj, key, value);
      │ ^
    7 │ d(obj, key);
    8 │ vue.set(obj, key, value);
  
  i Vue 3 detects added and deleted properties on its own, so this function no longer exists and calling it throws an error.
  
  i Assign the property directly instead, for example object.key = value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

